 "remarks": "For offer is a 2 BR, 1 BTH 900 sq ft unit in need of tender loving care with great potential. Located in River Haven, an established owner-centric co-op, within an amenity-rich location and the center of downtown Stamford a short stroll away. The complex is uniquely positioned in a residential neighborhood offering affordable and accessible entry into one of the most competitive housing markets in the nation. With a little bit of paint and a world of ideas, the talented individual can return the charm and transform interior of a front facing unit into a cozy, loving, incredible home. Past vestiges remain -- a recessed laundry hamper in the bathroom, the tiny vestibule with overhead storage entering the main bedroom, and right outside the windows are two American beauties, the treetops of a stately Elm one one end and a turning Maple on the other, where you'll get a glimpse of the horizon in the distance. Onsite laundry, resident's only parking (including three electric chargers), seasonal patio out back. Great walkability and very short distance to a plethora of restaurants, entertainment, schools, shopping, public transportation, Mill River, Scalzi and Colombus Parks, Stamford Hospital, Target, UCONN, library, Metro North and host of annual events the city is known for.  Owner occupancy only, no investors. Board requires a maximum 34 debt to income ratio. Heat, hot water and taxes included in HOA. Unit sold as is.",
